  "answer_text": "Elena Gilbert turns into a vampire across the **Season 3 finale and the Season 4 premiere** of *The Vampire Diaries*:\n\n* **The Death / Transition Begins:** **Season 3, Episode 22 (\"The Departed\")**\n* **The Transition Completes:** **Season 4, Episode 1 (\"Growing Pains\")**\n\n### How it happens:\n1. **The Vampire Blood:** Earlier in the Season 3 finale, Elena suffers a brain injury. To save her, Dr. Meredith Fell secretly treats her using Damon Salvatore\u2019s vampire blood. \n2. **The Accident:** Later in the episode, Rebekah Mikaelson stands in the middle of Wickery Bridge, causing Matt Donovan to swerve his truck\u2014with Elena in the passenger seat\u2014off the bridge and into the water.\n3. **The Sacrifice:** Stefan Salvatore arrives to rescue them from the drowning vehicle. Elena insists that Stefan save Matt first. Stefan respects her wishes, but by the time he returns for Elena, she has drowned. \n4. **Waking Up:** Because Elena died with Damon's vampire blood still in her system, she wakes up on a slab in the morgue at the very end of the Season 3 finale. \n5. **Completing the Transition:** In the Season 4 premiere, Elena struggles with the choice of whether to complete her transition or let herself die. Eventually, after being locked up by the Founder's Council, Stefan helps her feed on human guard blood, completing her transformation into a vampire.\n\n*(Note: Elena eventually becomes a human again in the Season 6 finale, \"I'm Thinking of You All the While,\" after taking the cure for vampirism.)*",
